Internal Use Only

This repository is an internal knowledge base for Get Sweaty Games. Its contents
(department knowledge, canonical docs, and org-specific conventions) are proprietary
and not licensed for external use or distribution.

The underlying folder-structure methodology this repo is built on is adapted from the
Interpretable Context Methodology (ICM) by Jake Van Clief
(https://github.com/RinDig/Interpretable-Context-Methodology), originally released under
the MIT License. That license continues to cover the general methodology/pattern approach
itself, not the specific department content maintained in this repository.
